// Every ability word shares one body: the italicized label wraps whatever
// ability follows it [CR#207.2c]. `params`/`body` are hardcoded here rather
// than left as per-file params: every declaration takes exactly one
// `Ability` argument and wraps it the same way, so there is nothing for a
// file to override. `Quote(Param(0))` defers that hole past this
// meta-expansion to the produced declaration's own frame, where a real
// invocation resolves it against its own positional argument.
//
// `kinds` stays `[AbilityWord]` only, matching every sibling declaration
// family: `deckmaste_construction_core::macro_def::normalized_kind` requires
// exactly one kind per declaration (`let [kind] = definition.kinds.as_slice()
// else { ... InvalidDeclarationKind }`), so a second kind here breaks the
// english_v2/semantics_v2 shared-contract drift test. This means the
// produced macro cannot be invoked as `Adamant(<ability>)` at a card's
// `Ability` position — confirmed empirically (`InvalidDeclarationKind`) —
// exactly the "name-erasing loader tag" behavior `ron.rs`'s
// `DECLARATION_KINDS` doc comment already ascribes to this family. Widening
// that is a `deckmaste_construction_core` change outside this ticket.
(
    name: "AbilityWord",
    kinds: [Macro],
    params: {
        "name": String,
        "spelling": String,
        "grammar": Elidable(Any),
    },
    body: (
        name: Param(name),
        kinds: [AbilityWord],
        params: [Ability],
        metadata: (
            spelling: Param(spelling),
            grammar: Param(grammar),
        ),
        body: ItalicHead(word: AbilityWord(label: Param(name)), ability: Quote(Param(0))),
    ),
)
